== reading ==
1. ffi 0 and ffi-hosttc 0 in EVERY row of both planted builds: the control never shows the ffi arm can fail.
2. 'roundtrip' decodes through the core and RE-ENCODES WITH ak::Enc, so it is the planted native encoder
   observed a second time: native N and roundtrip N are always equal. The pad build's T6 two-shape row
   '44 wrong' is 22 distinct wrong encodes (native 22 + the same 22 again); T2/T3 '46 of 96' is 23.
3. The T6 labels are typed and wrong: g_shapes is P1.1, P1.3, P1.2, P2.2 (T0 reordered it), so
   'one shape (P1.2 alone)' is P1.3 alone and 'two shapes (P1.1 + P1.2)' is P1.1 + P1.3.
